hy I kept watch over the corpse all night.\" [3495] \"There's no place to go out at night around here, so it's unnatural to have an alibi!\" Miyuki said. [3496] It seems that Mei Mei also doesn't have an alibi. [3497] \"Did you stay at home after returning at 7 pm, Mei Mei?\" asked the hopeless. [3498] \"Yes. I prepared dinner when I got home and ate around 8 pm. After that, my parents watched TV, and I put aside the dishwashing work and read books and stared into space in my room. Even though my house is a small bungalow, my parents probably wouldn't notice if Romeo came to tempt me out.\" [3499] Compared to the first conversation with Mei Mei, she is much more open now, probably because it is easier to get along with peers of the same age. Almost no male peers of our age are seen in this village. [3500] \"You were alone in your room, so your alibi shouldn't stand. \"Hopeless said casually, \"Even if you propose that the three of us were together, the police won't believe your parents' testimony.\" [3501] The fragrance of Darjeeling tea, the pleasant sound of a spoon hitting a cup, and the relaxed conversation about the murder case. Although it was a long afternoon, the detectives must be out in the gloomy weather, trying to arrest the killer. [3502] \"Have you heard the news on the radio?\" [3503] Mei Mei mentioned the news that was broadcasted during our sleep. The news reported that \"Mr. Mori was possibly involved in a transaction and killed.\" [3504] Mr. Mori's attempt to get an exclusive interview with Ms. Senjyu was suppressed by the police. It's hard to imagine that the \"incident\" he got involved in has nothing to do with Mukumura village. [3505] \"The detectives are investigating everywhere in the village. This is the biggest commotion since the village was established, and even reporters have come to the village. Although they are asking around to find suspicious people, if there really is a suspicious person in the village, the news will spread quickly