 said it, what then?\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 6:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:47:05 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nIt was not the two-headed dragon living in the Dragon River, but a flood, but for some reason, it had countless hands...\n[1753] \"This...\"\n[1754] It looked like a forest breaking through the waves. The hands that emerged from the rapids turned out to be uprooted cypress trees. It must have been two days and two nights of continuous rain that uprooted the entire cypress forest and rushed into the river. Due to the large amount of rainwater and the entire cypress forest rushing into the river, the river burst its banks and roared downstream. [1755] \"Oh no!\" [1756] Wada put the car into reverse, but the cedar tree torrent had reached the bridge, and the bridge broke apart as quickly as disposable chopsticks. Several tree roots faced upwards flew into the air and landed on the riverbank. The car still didn't start, and the torrent was about to approach, carrying tree trunks and making a dull sound as they collided with each other. The scene was less than ten meters away from us. I felt like I was witnessing a train from hell crashing through. [1757] When the car retreated to a place where the water splashed couldn't reach, the broken logs almost went with the current. But Wada continued to reverse. [1758] \"Kozu, look behind us!\" [1759] \"It's already over, the water has receded!\" I shouted. [1760] \"Maybe it'll come back, run away!\" I followed his advice. [1761] The overflowing river formed small waves that surrounded the car's undercarriage, but we still drove out of the mountain road safely. When we stopped the car at the center of the three-way intersection, a late fear made us look at each other with trembling. [1762] \"The bridge fell down,\" Oda said, resting his chin on the steering wheel. \"Did you see it?\" [1763] \"I saw it. It just snapped like that\u2026\"\n[1764] I finally understood what it meant - we couldn't go to Mukimura. Although the dice had been thrown, we were ready to get involved in the incident, and now we couldn't cross the Rubicon (note: the Rubicon is a river in northern Italy. In 49 BC, Julius Caesar and the Senate plotted to attack Caesar, and the Rubicon was the border between Caesar's territory and the Italian mainland. Caesar defied everything and led his army across the river to fight Pompey.) [1765] \"We can't go there.\" [1766] \"Not only that, but the Jang Shrine and Matsuriya can't come out either?\" [1767] \"Ah!\" [1768] It was only then that I realized this. Yes! Mukumuku village is now completely isolated. [1769] \"Sensei, there's still a way! Phone!\" [1770] \"No, it won't work either! The wires and phone lines should have been washed away!\" [1771] \"You couldn't even receive any contact from Reverend Koji?\" [1772] \"Anyway, it's all like this 'kakuzi' sound\u2026\" Oda spoke as he made a gesture of cutting with scissors in the air, as if the air itself was making a sound and being cut. [1773] \"Let's try again!\" I felt a wave of impatience, \"Let's try calling the inn again. Maybe it will go through!\" [1774] \"Should we try?\" Oda roughly turned the steering wheel, and the car's direction changed accordingly. The car was fine and started smoothly. [1775] We hurried back. [1776] \"Hey, you're back so quickly!\" Wakatsuki was surprised to see us rushing back to the room. Despite his grumbling, he took Weidita's book to pass the time. [1777] \"The bridge is broken.\" [1778] \"What bridge?\" [1779] I couldn't wait to explain to him and rushed to the phone, trying to dial the number I had memorized. [1780] No response. [1781] \"As expected, it didn't work.\" I slumped my shoulders and hung up the phone that didn't even make a \"ding\" sound. [1782] What's going on? [1783] \"Strange...\" I picked up the phone again and dialed my home in Osaka. [1784] Wakayama asked curiously, \"Where are you calling?\" [1785] There was still no sound, and the dial tone didn't come through. [1786] Asakusa took the phone from me, tried it, and then shook his head. Weitada then took the phone. [1787] It doesn't matter who dials it, I thought, as I turned on the TV. [1788] We were all surprised when we found out we couldn't turn it on. [1789] \"Is it a power outage?\" [1790] This rain seems to have cut off Osakura Village's connection to the outside world. [1791] Chapter 7: The Death in the Dark Room - Yotsuba\n[1792] 1\n[1793] We stood silently side by side. [1794] Nakatani Kunio took the chopsticks first and said, \"Don't be so discouraged. Let's eat!\" [1795] We responded with a \"Okay\" and followed suit, picking up our chopsticks. I noticed that we all had hunched backs, so I straightened my chest. Lastly, Minami, who served the tea, sat slumped beside Dr. Nakatani. [1796]We were invited to the clinic for lunch. [1797]\"The experience was truly terrifying! It must have been like a near-death experience,\" said the thin doctor as he scooped some mashed potato into his mouth. He was around forty years old and his hair was quite sparse. [1798]\"I didn't know what was happening when I heard that strange sound. The river has flooded before, so I thought it might be a flood.\" [1799]Dr. Kotai hails from a village upstream of the Dragon Forest River, also known as Dragon Forest. His grandparents died in a flood. He is the eldest son of three and was a top scholar in the village. After graduating from junior high school, he was sent to a relative's house in Kobe until he graduated from medical school. He worked at a county hospital for ten years, got married during that time, but eventually divorced without children. He was invited to this village clinic after the passing of the previous doctor. [1800] \"Cypress trees can't take root, and they often can't withstand heavy rain, falling over instantly. I remember a severe disaster in Kyushu a few years ago. The slopes covered with cypress trees were really dangerous!\" Dr. Kotai spoke without stopping, despite having a mouthful of food. [1801] I recalled seeing the cypress trees flowing under the bridge the day before. Perhaps it was a premonition of the mountain collapsing! [1802] \"The electronic clock stops when there is a power outage. It's now 12:30. The power and phone should be restored soon. I hope it's back by evening,\" Dr. Nakagawa said calmly. [1803] When we found out that the phone and power were affected, we were worried that Sumiya village might become an island due to landslides, but the situation was not that severe. Although several small landslides caused power lines to be cut, vehicles were not completely inaccessible - although it was said that they were prohibited due to safety concerns - this information was announced by a police car from the Sumiya police station. Repair work has begun, but it will probably continue until evening. [1804] \"The people of Mokumegura must be more worried! Not only is the bridge broken, but the phone and power lines are also cut off, and there is no way to get any information from anywhere...\"\n[1805] Although Miyuki is right, there is nothing we can do about it. Even if we want to rebuild the bridge, it will probably take a long time given the condition of this road.\" [1806] \"Mokuzu Village should be fine. The terrain there is higher than here, so it shouldn't be flooded.\" [1807] \"How was the doctor's cooking?\" Mayumi asked. [1808] We all spoke in unison like children: \"It was delicious.\" [1809] \"Doctor, what do you do before your evening clinic?\" Although not particularly interested, Wakatsuki opened the conversation. [1810] Dr. Nakahara took a bite of food and answered, \"I do some insurance-related things. I don't take naps. Oh! Today is a bit different. A photographer named Sugihara is coming.\" [1811] \"He said he has something to ask me. I thought that there wouldn't be much to discuss with a city photographer like me, but he insisted that I talk to him. It seems to be... related to Mukumura.\" [1812] \"Why does Sagihara want to know about Mukumura?\" Watanabe asked while fighting with natto. He usually doesn't eat this breakfast-like dish, but it appeared in the lunch menu in the depths of Tosa, and he was struggling to keep up. By the way, this is the first time I've eaten natto, and it's not as bad as I thought. [1813] \"Because I'm the only one who has been invited to the Mukumura big house. Sagihara wants me to tell him who's there and what life is like.\" [1814] We had already heard something similar yesterday. The teacher at the abandoned school \u2014 the one named Hijima \u2014 had mentioned that artists can also get sick. So it makes sense why Sagihara would come to interview Dr. Nakagawa, and he probably guessed that the doctor had been to the Mukumura big house! [1815]\n[1816] \"I've been called there a few times. Twice for colds, once for a dislocated shoulder after someone fell down the stairs. That's about it. However, I didn't go to see Miss Uma when she and her friends, especially Mizuki-san, had sprained ankles and fevers.\" [1817] \"People in the village said they wanted Dr. Nakamura to come, but Mizuki-san flatly refused,\" Mizuki added. [1818] Oda stopped eating and asked, \"Doctor, do you know about a former singer named Chikara Yoshizawa?\" [1819] \"Yes, I know!\" Dr. Nakamura nodded, and Mizuki nodded along beside him. [1820] Although doctors and nurses must maintain patient confidentiality, they may have deemed Yoshizawa not to be a patient or perhaps sensed that Oda's serious expression indicated a valid reason for his question. [1821] \"That photographer named Sagihara wanted to find out about Yuria from the doctor. He wanted to expose her hiding place to the public. That's what he said this morning.\" [1822] \"Oh!\" Doctor Nakatani showed a surprised expression, he didn't expect this. [1823] \"We really don't agree with his methods. Doctor, I'm asking you not to tell Sagihara about her!\" [1824] Takeda's passionate tone seemed to surprise the doctor and nurse. [1825] \"So that's the case. Well, I understand. Since it's like that, I won't say anything because I don't like it either. I know what Miss Chigusa has been through.\" [1826] I sighed in relief. At the same time, I felt satisfied that Sagihara's plan had been thwarted. Satoshi and Mei smiled with satisfaction, like children who had found a trap. [1827] \"Miss Senou had an eating disorder, but she has controlled her appetite now. To lose weight, she had to reduce her food intake significantly, and I told her to do it slowly so as not to damage her body. Overeating and anorexia are common eating disorders among women. It's a 'sudden urge to destroy one's own appearance.' For women, appearance is of great importance! That's why Miss Senou was so miserable and upset. It's really heartbreaking to see a popular idol suffer from this illness.\" [1828] Last night, when we sneaked into the garden behind the Uzuki Mansion, a woman with a round face peered out of the second-floor window. The woman who screamed when she saw us was probably Uzuki by the name of Senou. I might not have recognized her even in broad daylight because I didn't expect an idol to live there, and the round contours...\n[1829] \"How many people are there in the village of Uzuki?\" Mei asked. Even this information was unknown to outsiders. [1830] Dr. Nakamura stared at the ceiling, \"Eleven.\" [1831] \"Does that include Matsuri?\" asked Oda. [1832] \"Yes. Including your seniors, there are twelve people. Many people think there should be more villagers, but that's not the case. They are just people with a small plot of land that is similar to a family garden. The focus seems to have been blurred. If they are busy farming all day, they probably don't have time to draw.\" [1833] \"Do the people of Mukae Village really have no contact with the people of Sumi Village?\" I asked. [1834] \"Almost none. Although they also go out to buy daily necessities at the convenience store, most of them go to other towns like Sugi or Tsukuba to buy things. The people who come out are of various shapes and sizes, but only Ms. Senou seems to have never left the village.\" [1835] \"So, no one knows that Ms. Senou lives in Mukae Village, right?\" [1836] \"Probably only me and Mei. There should be no one else.\" [1837] So who told Sagihara about Miss Seno living in Matsukura village? These two don't seem like they're lying. As I was thinking about this, I suddenly remembered something. \"Is the mail delivered directly to the mansion?\" [1838] \"There are many things listed as mail, but some are delivered there. There is a mailbox the size of a postbox at the bridge.\" [1839] I remember seeing that mailbox. \"Is the mail delivered by the local post office?\" [1840] \"Hmm, yes. It's Mr. Shigemori. Me and Mr. Shigemori are the only ones who can cross the bridge legally.\" [1841] Does Shigemori not know? I think he might have leaked the secret to Suguru. But what does it matter? - It would be troublesome if he thinks the same thing! [1842] After finishing our meal, we also drank coffee and chatted for a while. It's actually impolite because Suguru's visit is almost upon us. [1843] We left the clinic before 2 pm, and although the rain has slowed down, it seems it doesn't want to stop. [1844] \"Look!\" Wakayama urged me to look in the direction of the hotel, and I saw Suguru approaching us, and it seems he noticed us. We politely nodded and passed by each other. When we looked back, he was standing in front of the clinic, glancing in our direction. Our eyes met. \"One move short!\" [1845] Wakayama said, \"Hmm, he probably saw us come out. You didn't see the expression on his face that wanted to ask 'Why are these guys at the clinic'?\" [1846] \"The midwife should give him a one-two-three punch!\" Shizu said cheerfully. The fan of Sen no Tsuyu seemed happy. [1847] 2\n[1848] Since our stay will probably be extended, we need to withdraw the funds, so we went to the post office. In a rural trip where credit cards cannot be used, the post office deposit is the most convenient, so we stored all the money in Wakagi's post office account and left Kyoto. [1849] This is an old and small post office. Even among the specific post offices, it may be one of the few in the country. The counter and pillars have a golden yellow sheen, and there are only three employees inside. While Wakagi was withdrawing money, I stared blankly at the pension, small package delivery, and postcards, and realized that I didn't know the date today. [1850] \"Are you Mr. Shirogami?\" [1851] I turned around and saw a man with curly hair and a slightly older age than us squinting with his eyes apart. \"Yes,\" he said. [1852] \"We heard that you deliver mail to Mukumura village... Ah, I'm sorry to suddenly say this. We were just chatting with the midwife, and he told us that there is a Shitomori-san who delivers mail to Mukumura village.\" [1853] \"Yes. The clerk in charge of the office is sick and on leave, so I had to work at the window yesterday and today. Actually, I'm a mail carrier. Is there anything wrong?\" [1854] - Shitomori seemed to be saying, \"What do you want to say?\" [1855] \"We're interested in Mukumura village. It was introduced in the magazine, so we thought we might as well stop by when we came here. We were chased away, but it made us even more curious about the situation inside! Can you tell us something about the situation inside? I heard that the only people who have gone to Mukumura village from Sumiura village are the midwife and Shitomori-san...\"\n[1856] \"Ah!\" The post office clerk seemed quite serious as he sighed, \"I didn't go to the main house when I delivered things there, so I don't know the inside. I just deliver mail, and I don't know who's inside.\" [1857] \"You don't know at all?\" [1858] \"I recognize a few faces and greet them, but that's all.\" [1859] \"Do you know a chubby young girl?\" [1860] \"Is there such a girl? There is a cute red-haired girl recently, but she's not fat!\" [1861] Red hair! It's Malya, who has been like the plot of \"Please Ask for Your Name\" (note: a movie adapted from the novel by Kataoka Ihei, with three episodes, and \"Please Ask for Your Name\" is the second unit. It describes how the two characters, Shizuko and Shinji, save each other without exchanging names and agree to meet again in six months. Since then, these two people have never forgotten each other, but they have always missed each other. The whole movie is about the process of their missing each other.) who kept missing each other. When I think that this clerk has seen Malya, my chest hurts slightly. [1862] \"Excuse me...,\" Ochiai interjected, \"You said you didn't go to the mansion, but if the mail you sent is too big to fit in the mailbox, what should you do? It should be delivered there, right?\" [1863] \"No, I'll call first, and then someone will come to pick it up in a car.\" [1864] \"I see.\"\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 7:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:47:05 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nI came here because... well, I suppose I can only say that I didn't adapt to city life. I don't have any relatives or acquaintances here either...\"\n[831] Suma no Mura is not just the village where we are currently staying, but also includes five other villages within a six-kilometer radius. \"The village\" is a much larger administrative unit than I imagined. The population of Suma no Mura, which includes five villages, is said to be 1,800 people. Since the size and population of the five villages are not far apart, it is difficult to distinguish them, so the village office, police station, and school are scattered in various locations. This Suma no Mura, named after the settlement of Suma, has a post office, clinic, and elementary school, but the school is facing closure due to declining population. Mr. Yuriwajima, a teacher, is concerned about the population loss in the mountains of Kochi Prefecture, sighing over people's one-sided concentration on Tokyo and even discussing the necessity of moving the capital. He is truly a teacher. [832] \"Although the village office is elsewhere, this village has a clinic! It's much more difficult to set up a clinic than a police station, which is probably not needed much in such a leisurely place. Doctors are very popular. It is said that the clinic has been located in the village of Suma since the beginning.\" [833] \"It's not without reason. In such a peaceful place, there may not be many occasions when police are needed. Doctors are very popular. It is said that the clinic has been located in the village of Suma since the beginning.\" [834] This is not without reason. In such a peaceful place, there may not be many occasions when police are needed. Doctors are very popular. It is said that the clinic has been located in the village of Suma since the beginning.\" [835] \"I heard that before, another doctor was practicing here. After the previous doctor passed away due to old age, the village offered a house to recruit a successor. The current Doctor Nakahara agreed to come here under these conditions. This is what I heard, because Doctor Nakahara came here before me... He is very friendly and is greatly loved by the villagers. There is also a beautiful and gentle nurse at the clinic, making people feel that it's worth getting sick to see her.\" [836] After jokingly saying something for the first time, Mr. Higashi laughed like an old man, \"Haha, haha.\" From the first impression, he did not seem like a talkative person, but this country teacher was able to change the topic and talk enthusiastically. [837] \"The original residents of Mashiki village left the area about twelve years ago, so it became an abandoned village. It is not without reason that the land on the other side of the Dragon River is more inconvenient than here. It is not without reason that it became an abandoned village. [838] \"When talking about the Dragon River... I have heard from my students that there is a legend about it. The most common version is that a dragon that eats people lived on the river a long time ago. The dragon threatened the villagers, demanding that they sacrifice a girl every harvest season as a tribute. If they did not comply, it would cause the river to flood and destroy the entire village. The dragon would create a storm to urge the villagers. The villagers on this side of the river and those on the other side, now known as Mashiki village, agreed to alternate in providing the sacrifice. The villagers on the other side of the river first selected a woman as the sacrifice, but the storm did not subside. As the villagers were at a loss for what to do, a person appeared... You guess who it is?\" [839] \"Is it Tsukuyomi no Mikoto (a.k.a. Sukuna-hikona-no-mikoto, the younger brother of Amaterasu Omikami, the god of the sea, who killed the eight-headed serpent that devoured young girls in Utsunomiya Province)?\" Watanabe spoke seriously. [840] \"No, this is Shikoku!\" [841] \"I know!\" Jinguji-sensei said confidently, \"It's the Great Teacher Kobo Daishi!\" [842] Oshima laughed again, \"You got it right! At that time, it was the Great Teacher Kobo Daishi who appeared in Shikoku. After he defeated the dragon with the power of Buddhism, it was found out why the girl handed over by the village on the other side could not satisfy the dragon. It turned out that the dragon had two heads! The dragon's purpose of causing chaos was to make both villages sacrifice someone. [843] It was ridiculous to talk about a two-headed dragon against Kobo Daishi. However, we still expressed our astonishment politely. [844] \"Some people say that the original form of the eight-headed serpent in Uwakai River is the flooding of the Dragon Forest River. From this legend, we can also infer that the Dragon Forest River is a river prone to flooding. It still often floods...\n[845] Oshima looked up at the dark sky, \"It seems like it's going to rain again, so we need to be more vigilant.\" I also looked up at the dark sky, hoping to rescue the princess on the other side before it rained. [846] \"If you don't mind, I would like to invite you to my humble abode - the house next to the clinic - to sit down. However, I am a widower living alone, and my house is quite messy...\"\n[847] After leaving Motsu-jima, we played some more cards. Eventually, J\u014dsen-sensei said he wasn't feeling well and couldn't perform his big wheel routine. [848] 4\n[849] This village called Sumizu has a school, clinic, post office, and guesthouse, as well as a restaurant called \"Fukuzushiya.\" The lunch menu at this restaurant features a \"Fukuzushi\" set meal that lives up to its name, and it's also a social hub in the village. In the evenings, it transforms into a lively pub. If this were in a British countryside mystery novel, it would probably be introduced with a name like \"The Dharma Master's Sanctuary.\" Our hangovers had subsided, and a fierce hunger overtook us, so we enjoyed the Fukuzushi set meal at the restaurant near the entrance of the village. [850] The door opened, and I immediately put down my chopsticks. It was Sora Hiroki. [851] \"This is the only restaurant in town, and I can see you're all here. Boss, one Fu Shou set meal!\" [852] \"One Fu Shou set meal\" is a way of ordering for regular customers. Naito Naoki probably solves most of his lunches here. He sat down at our six-seat table, put down his camera on his shoulder. [853] \"It was really noisy just now. I was defeated by that guy! Look, my wrists are all swollen.\" [854] \"We have already explained the purpose of our visit to Mukumuku Village, but we don't know why Naito-san went there. Was it to find better shooting 