e subject. \"It might rain later, Mr. Kusanagi. Do you have any plans for afterwards, and any more photos to take?\" [866] \"Hmm, yes. I want to get back early in case we get stuck in the mountains. I'm planning to stay one more night and then end the trip. Are you not planning to leave?\" [867] \"Hmm.\" [868] \"Oh, I see... Although it may be difficult to enter Mukumuku village, I hope you have a safe journey.\" [869] \"Mr. Ibaragi.\" [870] Mr. Ibaragi turned his head slightly when he heard Mr. Ibaragi call out formally. \"Ah!\" he exclaimed. [871] \"Do you mean...there are people in Mugino village that Mr. Aoyama knows?\" [872] The question seemed to catch Mr. Aoyama off guard, and he couldn't answer immediately. However, he quickly put on a false smile and denied it, \"I don't know what made you think that. In fact, I don't even know anyone in Shikoku, let alone Mugino village.\" [873] Since it seemed impossible to extract any more information from him, the senior priest didn't press further but asked, \"Is there a public phone in this village? I'd like to try calling Mugino-san.\" [874] \"I don't think so. Boss, is there a public phone in the village? Is there a post office?\" [875] A voice from behind the door curtain in the kitchen answered, \"There's no public phone, and the telephone penetration rate in this village is 100%.\" [876] \"Oh, we can just use the phone at the inn. Dial '0' to connect to an outside line. You can look up the phone number in the inn's phone book.\" [877] Professor Yamamura simply says, \"Let's do that.\" [878] Mr. Umezawa has already provided us with the phone number. [879] The meal is over, so we can only go back to the inn. Mr. Maezono also leaves with us. [880] 5\n[881] We are in our hotel room. [882] Mr. Onizuka is holding the phone, and I am standing next to him, reading out the phone number written in my notebook. Kouyama, Ochiai, and Yasuhara are also leaning in to listen. Despite having nothing to do with it, Yasuhara seems 