here might be errors in the search, and if the police really believed that Sugiyama was called out by someone, he would have no suspicion as he had never had direct contact with him.\" [4669] \"So he arranged an alibi for 9 pm?\" [4670] \"The teacher and we were chosen by Shima to be witnesses. It doesn't matter who it is, as long as the Fukuju House is still open, even if there are no customers, the owner of the store can be a witness, so Shima went into the store.\" [4671] \"So we tracked down Shiroku's criminal behavior.\" [4672] \"The only remaining question that is difficult to understand is the motive.\" [4673] \"Hmm. What kind of transaction were they planning to do? This seems to be a key point, but we don't know.\" [4674] \"Araoka wasn't holding 'that thing' at the abandoned school? Since there was no suspicious item left at the scene, then...\"\n[4675] \"Anyway, I think it should be a photo.\" Watanabe concluded. \"Why?\" Dr. Nakahara leaned forward like a turtle. [4676] \"The film in the camera left at the scene was taken, wasn't it? That film should be the most suspicious!\" [4677] \"That's not necessarily true.\" Wakamatsu blocked Watanabe's path, \"Perhaps Sagihara just pointed the camera at the killer who came, took a snapshot, and that's why the killer couldn't ignore it. It has nothing to do with the original deal.\" [4678] \"That's true. However\u2026 when we talk about the thing Sagihara was supposed to hand over, we naturally think of his photos. If we remove the 'photographer' characteristic from Sagihara, he's just an ordinary person. So Roomi should want Sagihara to hand over some photos\u2026\"\n[4679] \"But Sagihara took pictures of the scenery of Dragon River or sunset scenes, didn't he? Roomi has no reason to want those things.\" [4680] \"Of course. The photos Sagihara was asked for the night before on the phone were something else. But after Roomi killed Sagihara and took that thing, he might have thought that there might be similar photo