ed doctor's kind offer and watched him leave to refill his cup. Just then, the phone rang. [4694] \"Hello? This is Middle-aged Doctor.\" [4695] I could see the middle-aged doctor's silhouette holding a coffee cup with one hand while answering the phone. It's probably a patient with an urgent need for a house call. [4696] \"How is it?\" Midori's voice suddenly became urgent, causing us to look at each other, \"I'm coming right away!\" [4697] He hung up the phone and rushed back to us with an empty cup. [4698] \"Suzuki was injured!\" [4699] 3\n[4700] Midori held a medical bag in his left hand and rolled up the front of his white coat with his right hand, jumping onto the car that came to pick him up. As we watched him go, the police car spewed exhaust into the night air, heading up the mountain. [4701] The phone call was from the police station in the village of Ryujin, Mr. Nakatani's hometown. Apparently, Shimizu had walked nearly two hours to the neighboring village. He was said to have been hiding in an abandoned police observation post in the outskirts of the village, where he was questioned by patrol officers and then fled into the mountains. However, he slipped and fell into a stream. Although he had been taken to the police station, his injuries were severe, and moving him would be dangerous to his life, so the police called Mr. Nakatani and came to pick him up. [4702] As we watched the tail lights of the police car go, not only us, but also the villagers were watching. Information like \"We already know who killed the photographer,\" \"It seems to be the postman Shimizu,\" \"He fled into the mountains,\" \"The fire department is mobilized,\" \"He was caught,\" and so on, spread like lightning, causing a stir in the village at night. [4703] After the car that took Mr. Nakatani left, villagers came out of their houses one after another, gathering in various places to exchange incomplete information, and unconsciously raising their voices. [4704] \"It's really terrifying!\" [4705] \"Why did Shimizu do such a thing?\" [4706] Just as I realized that an elderly couple was talking behind me, I saw the crowd surrounding the firefighters who had retreated from the mountains and were some distance away from us, asking questions. We stood alone by the roadside, finding it difficult to leave this unusual atmosphere and return to the inn. [4707] At this time, other police cars that had come to the scene drove towards Saito's house. Upon hearing the siren of the police car, several more people rushed outside. The commotion did not show any signs of calming down but rather gradually spread. [4708] \"Let's go take a look?\" Wakamatsu pointed to where the police car was parked. His implication was that \"If you don't go, I'll go myself.\" Naturally, Yoshida and I, who loved to see a good show, did not object. [4709] Nishimura and the innkeeper's wife stood side by side in front of the inn, probably coming out to investigate the unexpected commotion. [4710] \"I heard that Saito-san was arrested?\" Nishimura quietly approached us. [4711] Wakamatsu informed him that not only was Uchiyama arrested, but he was also injured, which is why Doctor Nakamura went to the village of Tsukiyama. [4712] Nishimura's eyes widened in surprise behind his glasses. \"But more police cars are arriving here. What's going on?\" [4713] \"We don't know either, so we decided to go take a look,\" Wakamatsu said. [4714] After hearing this, Nishimura naturally joined our group. [4715] In front of the Uchiyama residence, which was surrounded by a narrow courtyard with a hawthorn hedge, two police cars were parked. The revolving headlights cast a red glow on the crowd gathered around the crime scene. A rope marked \"Do Not Enter\" was placed at the entrance. [4716]\"Get away! Get away! Don't obstruct the investigation!\" [4717]The voice reminding the villagers near the house sounds familiar. Looking in the direction of the crowd, I meet the gaze of Detective Fujimura. It's really him! [4718]\"Ah! It's you guys!\" Fujimura raises his hands in excitement. [4719]As I ponder, his hands wave us over. We wonder what's going on and push our way through the crowd. Westwell follows with a \"I guess I'm one of them\" expression, crossing the cordoned-off area. Under the curious gaze of the villagers, we enter the courtyard. [4720]\"As you said, before receiving a call from Officer Hasegawa of Longsen, Shimo confessed.\" Fujimura covers his mouth with one hand and whispers. [4721] \"He confessed? We heard he suffered serious injuries.\" [4722] Fujisawa turned around, facing away from the crowd, and we followed suit. \"It's not a fatal wound, and he probably thinks he can't escape. Thanks to you, we managed to prevent him from escaping, and the case is now temporarily resolved. We also confirmed that the time specified on the note was 7:00.\" [4723] \"What? What's going on?\" I was surprised again by my own accurate deduction. [4724] \"Actually, we examined the note left in the room at Suwa's house, the one on top of the stack of white paper. Upon closer inspection, there were still traces of his handwriting. Under the light, it was possible to see the words 'Meet you at 7:00.' Just as you all deduced, the murderer of Shigemori Naotaka is Shigemori Daisuke.\" [4725] \"I'm glad to hear it's not some nonsense,\" said Nishijima seriously. He really seemed to believe it! [4726] \"So we're going to search his house thoroughly next?\" [4727] The detective's mutterings were overheard by the police, \"We've already been searching thoroughly since just now. It's still a suspicious case because there's a strange thing.\" [4728] \"Strange thing?\" Everyone asked. [4729] \"Yeah, it's quite shocking!\" [4730] Even Fujisawa, who remained calm even when alone, asked impatiently, \"What is it?\" [4731] \"We found... well, a human ear from the drawer of the desk!\" [4732] We were taken aback by such an unexpected item and couldn't respond for a moment. [4733]